other gueses that were really close
and some of my other choice comments

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.240
later on.   Be sure to look out for some
secret subtitles and comment for your

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.360
chance to be featured.
Also, don't forget to rate, share and

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.960
SUBSCRIBE and click that Notification
Bell if you do enjoy it!  Although there

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.259
are ways to make the Mini Magic Balls
without tape, it's a lot more challenging

00:01:22.259 --> 00:01:25.796
and I'd like to show you the easiest way
I know first. I'm going to

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.070
a single sheet of 8.5 x 11"   
printer paper but if you want to use an

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:33.240
11'' by 17'' sheet just like this or even
tape two pieces of origami paper

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.620
together that's fine also.
So grab your sheet of paper and let's go!

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.000
To turn your paper into 1 to 2 (1:2)
proportion rectangle like this with two

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.060
connected squares, first fold it in half, lining up the edges perfectly.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.320
and making nice sharp creases set the
paper so that the vertical fold is a

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.340
mountain fold and then fold the corners
into the vertical midline like this and

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.780
then we could tear off the excess paper
on the bottom. Now that you have a paper

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.140
like this we're gonna flip it over and
fold these top two corners down to the

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.610
bottom also. Once again, making a nice
crease along the outside and do the same

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.750
with the upper left corner. Your paper
should now be twice as long as it is

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.900
wide with each square having an X in it.
Now your paper will be divided

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:18.909
in half along this vertical middle line
that is a mountain fold, also having two

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:23.560
X's on each side that I have marked with
dots (.) because this side is going to be

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.000
the outside or color side of the magic
ball.  The next thing we're going to do is

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.959
to split the paper into 16 vertical
sections just like this so let's go

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:35.650
ahead and do that. Take one end of the
paper and fold it on this vertical line

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:40.340
just like this across and then we're
going to hold it like this so that's the

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.980
two edges that are open are on the top
and take the top edge and fold

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.840
it down all the way to the bottom--again line it up as neatly as possible

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.520
and then make a crease along the top, running your
fingernail against it. Flip it over and

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.760
do the same exact thing: fold the top
edge down and crease sharply. Now when

00:02:56.769 --> 00:03:00.340
you open up the paper you see we split
the paper into quarters and we're going

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.420
to take these two folds now and fold
them directly into the middle so just

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.530
pinch that fold on the right side and
just slide it right into the middle line

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:13.180
and make a crease here all the way
throughout the paper and if you lift up

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.659
the outside right edge you'll see we
created a new fold here and let's do the

00:03:16.659 --> 00:03:20.709
same with the left side: slide the edge
directly into the middle and crease all

00:03:20.709 --> 00:03:23.889
the way down the paper. Now, your paper
will look something like this

00:03:23.889 --> 00:03:27.069
and we're going to take the outside
edges and also fold them directly into

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:30.549
the middle. Just take the edges one at
a time and fold them directly to the

00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:35.919
midline just like this *sings-do-do-do-do-do* Now you'll
see we split the paper into eight

00:03:35.919 --> 00:03:40.000
vertical sections. As you'll see the
paper now has three Mountain folds and

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.169
four valley folds, we're going to rotate
the paper and fold downwards on the

00:03:44.169 --> 00:03:49.060
valley folds. Crease downwards on all
of the valley folds across the paper

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:53.500
just like this. Once you've done that,
open the paper once more and turn it 90

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.549
degrees like this and take this first
mountain fold and slide it directly to

00:03:57.549 --> 00:04:02.139
the middle line--just pinch the mountain
fold like this and slide it down and

00:04:02.139 --> 00:04:06.069
once it's lined up then make a crease
directly in the middle of this next

00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:11.260
section here all the way across. That
basically creases the section in half as

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:15.609
you could see under here. Then we could
take the next section and split it in

00:04:15.609 --> 00:04:19.090
half by taking this mountain fold and
doing the same thing; so just take that

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:23.349
next mountain fold and fold it down
right on top of the previous one we just

00:04:23.349 --> 00:04:26.490
put in the middle, then let's flatten the
paper out.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.300
Then let's just keep doing that: fold this one in, just like this, and then finally fold the

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.169
very last edge into the middle trying to
be as neat as possible

00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:37.680
Now when you unfold everything you'll
see half of the paper is in sixteenths (1/16)

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.490
and now we could rotate the paper and do
the same thing with the other half just

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:45.090
like before take the mountain folds and
continue to bring them in to the middle

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.949
just like this take the last one and
just bring it down and then once you're

00:04:49.949 --> 00:04:53.849
done with that we could take the outside
edge and finally fold it into the middle

00:04:53.849 --> 00:04:57.990
once again give it a nice sharp crease.
Now we've split the paper into 16

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:02.310
vertical sections. Eventually, we will be
turning the vertical folds into mountain

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:06.020
folds. Now that we've divided it
vertically we can split it into eight

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:10.380
horizontal sections. First, we're going to
flip it on to the other side that's not

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:14.580
the "color side" just like this and just
flatten everything out. Then take the top

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.810
edge and fold it down to the bottom edge
and once they're aligned, we can crease (*Sound Effect*)

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.909
along that new top fold then we can just
crease the paper and open it up and

00:05:23.909 --> 00:05:27.780
we're going to take the top and the
bottom edges and fold it directly onto

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.979
the horizontal midline just like this.
When you do that, just make sure that

00:05:31.979 --> 00:05:36.979
each of the lines here lines up with the
rest of the fold. (*Sound Effects*)

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:43.490
Flip it upside down and then do the same
with the top, and as you'll see that line

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:49.370
that I drew is matching up with the
other side. You can unfold the paper and

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.910
flip it back over so that you have
something that looks just like this. All

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:57.500
horizontal creases are now Mountain
folds. Here is the horizontal middle line

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.370
and again we're going to take the first
Mountain fold here and fold it directly

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:05.390
in here by pinching it and sliding it
down directly into the middle and then

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:10.520
make a crease all the way across. Take
the outside edge and fold it down into

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:14.990
the middle also--taking your time and
being as neat as possible and lining up

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:19.610
all the creases. So fold it down, line it
up, and make a crease and now you flip it

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:23.540
around and do the same exact thing: Bring
the mountain fold directly into the

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.800
middle and flatten it out and then do
the same with the outside edge so if you

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:32.600
did that you should see an X with a
little bit of a box in the middle.  So now

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:36.230
again just run your fingernail against
the top and then we're basically just

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:41.300
going to fold the whole thing in half
just like this, so that it's kind of like a

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:45.140
fan. when you open up the paper you'll
see that we've split it into eight

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:49.669
different horizontal sections and 16
different vertical sections. To make the

00:06:49.669 --> 00:06:52.640
next step easier we're going to make
each of those vertical folds into

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.240
mountain folds so just take the paper
like this and fold it on each of these

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:00.380
creases just like that downwards to make
sure they're each Mountain folds. So just

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:05.320
keep folding down and creasing on each
one of the 16 sections to make sure that

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:09.200
it has a nice crease. To finish the pre
creases we need to make X's in every

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.320
single one of the boxes that we have on
the paper I'm also going to draw some

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.860
boxes just to make things easier for you
to see *Draws on Creases*

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:19.760
To turn this into this we need to

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.690
make all of the diagonal PRE-creases
going this way.and then all of the ones

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:27.830
going this way. I'm just going to draw
dots here so that it can help you

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:34.310
visualize what you need to be looking at
when you're making those creases. *Draws dots on intersections*

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:38.400
So as you'll see I drew dots at each of the
intersections going this way and all the

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:41.720
intersections going this way. What
you're going to first do is to take the

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:44.940
corner here and fold it to this dot. Then
you're going to take it and go to this

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.780
side this dot, this dot... all the way
through. We're going to do the same going this way.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.920
Start by taking the corner and
folding it into the first dot so that

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.240
this edge and this edge are aligned with with this one and this one, respectively.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:58.840
When you
do that, just make a nice sharp crease

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:02.750
and as you'll see not only are this edge
and this edge lined up with those two

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:07.430
lines that we drew, but this diagonal
line she'll also be in line with the one

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:11.080
that we have here. Then you can open it
up and then fold it into the second one--

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:15.460
make a nice sharp crease. At this point,
you'll see that this horizontal line

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.600
should be in line with this one and this
one should be in line with this one... so

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:22.550
there's just a couple of things that you
need to see when you do that just to

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:26.000
make sure everything is lined up nice
and neat then you can open it and do the

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.010
next one so fold it in to the third one.
Then we can continue to fold the corner

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:34.969
down to each intersection until we get
down to the bottom here. Make sure

00:08:34.969 --> 00:08:39.289
there's a nice crease on the fourth one.
Just make sure everything is lined up so

00:08:39.289 --> 00:08:42.770
now let's speed it up a little bit..(*Speed Increases*) just
continue to fold the corner down to each

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:47.270
dot on the diagonal line until you get
down to the bottom when we get down to

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:51.650
the bottom, you'll see we've already made
this diagonal fold across so we just

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:55.430
need to put the corner down and flatten
it out. Then we could fold the bottom

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:59.690
left corner to each one of these points
on this diagonal line. I just like to

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.020
flip the paper over because it's easier
for me, but you can do it whichever way

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:06.740
you like. Fold the corner to each
intersection of the boxes that I marked.

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:12.260
Be as neat as possible, lining up the
grid and making nice sharp creases.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:16.400
Now, you should have something that looks
like this, however we have not finished

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:22.040
all the pre creases that go in this
direction. You've only done up to here

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.550
--the corners-- so we just need to do the
seven (7) remaining ones in the middle so

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:29.780
I'll draw on the ones that we've already
done so you can see. At this point once

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:33.620
your paper looks like mine, you'll see
that we've done the creases all the way

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:38.870
down to the corners. So like I said we
just need to do the seven remaining ones

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:44.210
directly in the middle. If you look
closely, you'll see that this edge folds

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:48.800
directly on to the midline so all we
need to do is to shift the edge directly

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:54.650
to the left on this next vertical line.
So just shift that edge to the next or

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:59.150
adjacent vertical line and then we can
make a crease on the outside. Again,

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:04.220
following the same guidelines that these
horizontal lines are continuous with the

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:08.220
rest of the horizontal line on
left side of the paper. At this point

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:12.209
you'll notice that you have one row
that's overhanging on the bottom with

00:10:12.209 --> 00:10:15.690
this line coinciding with the very
bottom edge of the paper.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:19.709
Once you have it lined up like that, just
make a nice sharp crease all the way

00:10:19.709 --> 00:10:23.279
throughout and crease it with your
fingernail. So, it's going to go to the

00:10:23.279 --> 00:10:29.279
next one over: now you have two rows on
the bottom the second line here should

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:32.910
coincide with the bottom-- so make sure
all those lines are basically lined up

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:37.460
If you look at the bottom very closely,
you'll see that these diagonal folds

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:42.620
should coincide with the ones that are
already on this part of the paper as you

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:46.860
can see right here (*line*) so now we can crease
it and you'll see at the bottom we have

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:51.779
two rows hanging off. Then we can
continue to shift the edge over until

00:10:51.779 --> 00:10:55.709
there's four overhanging rows. So just so
you can see, I'm going to draw on the

00:10:55.709 --> 00:11:01.709
last four that we just did *Draws* and continue
to fold to these points now. Turn it over

00:11:01.709 --> 00:11:06.389
like this and once again we're going to
take this corner and fold it all the way

00:11:06.389 --> 00:11:11.070
down to the bottom of the paper. Since we
did four on this side, we know that we

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:15.959
have three (3) more left to do because there are only seven (7) in between the ones from

00:11:15.959 --> 00:11:20.250
corner to corner.  So, we just have to
basically get it down to here so we just

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:24.779
need through it three more times: there's
one,  there's two,  and three and there you

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.900
go you finished all the diagonal folds
going this way and again I'll draw on it

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:34.060
so that you could see which ones we've
done. So now you'll see we've done all of

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:38.480
the diagonal folds that are going in
this direction.  A good way to check to

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:42.690
see if you miss any fold is to look on
the back because Mountain folds are a

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:46.410
lot easier to see than Valley folds.  At
this point, you should have a piece of

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:49.980
paper that looks like this with all of
the diagonal pre creases in this

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:53.819
direction completed. We're now going to
do the diagonal pre creases in this (opposite)

00:11:53.819 --> 00:11:58.740
direction by taking these corners and
folding them inwards this way. Once we

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:02.910
get to the midline here, or at this point
here. We're then going to do the same

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:06.839
thing that we did in the other direction.
So let's go ahead and do that. Just like

00:12:06.839 --> 00:12:10.829
in the other direction: fold the corner
to each one of the dots on the line

00:12:10.829 --> 00:12:15.600
intersections. All the horizontal and
vertical folds should meet up--keep

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:19.560
folding until the corner reaches the
very bottom of the paper. Now I'm going

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:22.200
to flip it over and do the same with this corner.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:26.160
Once again, folding the corner down to each one of the intersections and aligning

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:31.950
the edges and folds. So now I will draw on
the pre creases that we just made: we now

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:36.270
have seven more pre-creases to make in
this direction. So just like before I'm

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:39.089
going to put the corner down and shift
it over to each one of these points,

00:12:39.089 --> 00:12:43.620
again making sure that all of the
creases align and that I have four rows

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:48.839
overhanging on the bottom. Once again, now that there's four overhanging rows on

00:12:48.839 --> 00:12:53.140
this side, we could flip it over and then
we're going to fold this corner down so

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:57.150
that there's three overhanging rows. (*3,2,1!!)

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:02.070
Great job! We just did all the PRE-
creases and every box should have an

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:09.450
"X"in it! So, as you'll see I have a grid
of 8 boxes by 16 boxes (8x16=?) and every single

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:14.280
one has an X in it. It's quite easy to
see this when you flip it over as well.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:18.029
You need to be very familiar with the
Water Bomb and that the diagonal folds in

00:13:18.029 --> 00:13:22.200
it are very sharp VALLEY folds. We're also
going to be dealing with something I

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:26.310
call the "Double Airplane Base" that looks
something like this and they're going to

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:29.840
be connected in this fashion. In this
larger scale you can see how the two

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:33.620
bases connect and that they'll flatten out and connect like so

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:38.540
You're going to have to be very familiar with this
pattern that has a waterbomb followed by

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:42.990
a double airplane base then next to
another water bomb that's connected to a

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:46.380
double airplane base.  In the columns
you'll see that the water bombs are

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:50.670
actually connected to each other there
are also staggered or offset which

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:55.350
creates a zigzag pattern. If you follow
along and pay close attention, with some

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:58.620
practice you'll definitely get it!
Although the lines I drew on the paper

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:03.750
show all the pre creases that we now
folded, not EVERY fold is necessary to

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:09.089
collapse the ball. So to avoid confusion
I outlined on this sheet the folds that

00:14:09.089 --> 00:14:13.200
we will need to collapse to make the
magic ball. *Remember* this side I am

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:18.240
holding UP will be the Outside or the
Color side of the magic ball. It's up to

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:21.930
you but you may want to go over the
diagonal creases in both directions and

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:26.310
also the mountain folds just because
it'll make it a little bit easier to

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:30.420
collapse the model. We're going to fan
out the model by first folding upwards

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:34.050
by Valley folding in the first crease
and then mountain folding and all

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:37.740
alternating all the way till you get
down to the bottom. When you look at it

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:42.000
from the side you'll see that you have
four V's (VVVV) connected to each other with

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.260
alternating Valley folds and mountain
folds. We will start working on the Mini

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:50.580
Magic Ball layer to layer, first creating
